<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Optional, off by default: the cerebrex art setting draws Odyssey's cerebrex node
    (Apparel_CerebrexNode) with this mod's art in place of Odyssey's. The node's art is two paths
    on the def: graphicData/texPath, the item on the ground and the icon the def resolves from
    it, and apparel/wornGraphicPath, the pack on the wearer's back (renderUtilityAsPack, so the
    worn path takes the facing suffixes and no body type one). Both take the one path of ours,
    which Mods/Odyssey/Textures carries as the item (no suffix) and the three worn facings, never
    at Odyssey's path, where it would replace the art for everyone.

    Our art ships masks where Odyssey's has none (_m for the item, _northm/_eastm/_southm for
    the worn pack, as the helmet's are named), so the patch also turns the two mask switches on:
    graphicData/shaderType CutoutComplex for the item and apparel/useWornGraphicMask for the
    pack (ApparelGraphicRecordGetter picks the worn shader from that flag, never from
    graphicData). The node is colorable (ApparelNoQualityBase's CompColorable), and without a
    mask a dye tints the whole piece: the masks paint the frame red and leave the core black, so
    a dyed node takes the color on its frame and keeps the red of its lens. An undyed node draws
    white through the mask and looks as it does without one. Odyssey's def sets neither field,
    so both are added.

    PatchOperationSetting reads the switch while the patches apply, so a change waits for a
    restart and the def then builds its graphic, icon and atlas entry from our path exactly as
    it would from Odyssey's; off, the patch touches nothing and Odyssey's XML stands. The root
    is gated on Odyssey's package id (LoadFolders.xml), so the xpaths never miss. The path here
    must match CerebrexNode.TexPath (Source/1.6/Settings/CerebrexNode.cs), which the settings
    window reads off the def to show which art is live; Tests/1.6/CerebrexNodeArtTests.cs holds
    the patch, that constant and the shipped textures together.
  -->
  <Operation Class="OverlordWarcasket.PatchOperationSetting">
    <setting>cerebrexArt</setting>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/graphicData/texPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/CerebrexNodeOverlord/CerebrexNodePack</texPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/apparel/wornGraphicPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/CerebrexNodeOverlord/CerebrexNodePack</wornGraphicPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/graphicData</xpath>
          <value>
            <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "Apparel_CerebrexNode"]/apparel</xpath>
          <value>
            <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
